---
import BaseLayout from '@shared/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Contact';
const description = 'Reach the CalcKDP team. We read every email — bug reports, feature requests, and feedback all welcome.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} pathname="/contact/" schemaType="WebPage">
  <article class="prose-like max-w-3xl space-y-4">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Contact</h1>

    <p>The fastest way to reach us is email:</p>
    <p class="text-lg"><a href="mailto:hello@kdp.cool" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">hello@kdp.cool</a></p>

    <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">We read everything — bug reports, feature requests, calculator suggestions, and corrections to the math or tax data are all welcome. Replies usually within a few days.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6">Found a bug?</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@kdp.cool" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">hello@kdp.cool</a> with the page URL, what you entered, what you expected, and what you got. Screenshots help.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6">Looking for a calculator we don't have?</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@kdp.cool" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">hello@kdp.cool</a>. We prioritize calculators that have a clear job, sources we can cite, and behavior we can show on the page.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6">What to include</h2>
    <p>For a calculator bug, include the page URL, the numbers you entered, the filing status or loan term if relevant, and the result you expected. Rounding differences can happen in financial calculators, so exact inputs help us distinguish a real formula issue from display rounding.</p>
    <p>For source corrections, include the official table, publication, or reference link. Tax and payroll pages are updated from published source data, not from screenshots or unsourced summaries.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6">Privacy note</h2>
    <p>Please do not send tax returns, Social Security numbers, pay stubs, bank statements, loan account numbers, or other sensitive personal documents. Use made-up numbers when possible; we only need enough detail to reproduce the calculator behavior.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
